{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_gefjtpsa5sskslcdxyefwwipaiy5retka5jnv4iukgb3oaletarq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 12 tests pass in both debug and release mode within the 60-second timeout. The translation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI translated the C SparseHash library to safe, idiomatic Rust:\n\n- **`SparseArray`**: Uses `Vec<SparseArrayGroup>` instead of raw `calloc`. Each `SparseArrayGroup` stores serialized elements in a `Vec<u8>` with a bitmap tracking occupancy. Uses `Vec::resize` and `copy_within` instead of `realloc`/`memmove`.\n- **`SparseDict`**: Uses a single-element `Vec<SparseArray>` since the C type holds one `*sparse_array`. Buckets are serialized as `[hash:8][klen:8][vlen:8][key][value]` byte sequences and stored inside the underlying sparse array — this avoids the C's bucket pointer trick while preserving the same probing/rehash semantics.\n- **Helpers**: `hash_fnv1a`, quadratic probing (`hash + n*n & (max-1)`), `position_to_offset` (using `count_ones()` for popcount), bitmap operations.\n- **No `unsafe`, no FFI**: Pure-Rust port; uses `to_ne_bytes`/`from_ne_bytes` to keep ABI parity with the C native-endian layout where it matters.\n\nAll 12 tests pass (including `test_dict_lots_of_set`, which inserts/retrieves 1M entries) within the 60-second timeout."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":642,"cache_read_input_tokens":47225,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":642,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c61ba03c-b63b-4bb0-85a8-ffc53efb23db","uuid":"a345c0cc-a864-41e0-b102-34ab52a9196f"}
